<title>USA: Octel says board approves rights changes.</title>
<headline>Octel says board approves rights changes.</headline>
<dateline>MILPITAS, Calif. 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Octel Communications Corp said on Friday that its Board of Directors has approved amendments to its common shares rights agreement.</p>
<p>Among other changes, the amendments boost the exercise price to $100 per right from $40, cut the redemption price to $0.001 per right from $0.01 and and extending the agreement term to August 29, 2006.</p>
</text>
